  "worked_solution": "First, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\,\\,(-4)\\,\\,}{(\\frac{1}{5})}=(-4)÷\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $-4=-\\frac{4}{1}$ and dividing by $\\frac{1}{5}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $\\frac{5}{1}.$ We can use these facts to simplify the fraction above:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)÷\\frac{1}{5} & = \\\\ (-\\frac{4}{1})\\times \\frac{5}{1} & = \\\\ -\\frac{4\\times 5}{1\\times 1} & = \\\\ -\\frac{20}{1} & = \\\\ -20 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\,\\,(-4)\\,\\,}{(\\frac{1}{5})}=-20.\n$$",
